<exercise>
<statement>
<p>State the order-theoretic definition of a lattice.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Give an example of a finite poset that is not a lattice and explain which
meet or join fails to exist.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that</p>

<p>
<md>\mathcal P(X)</md>
</p>

<p>is a lattice under inclusion.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that in <m>\mathcal P(X)</m>,</p>

<p>
<md>A\wedge B=A\cap B,\qquad A\vee B=A\cup B.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that the divisors of a fixed positive integer <m>n</m> form a lattice
under divisibility.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>For subspaces <m>U,W\leq V</m>, explain why</p>

<p>
<md>U\cap W</md>
</p>

<p>is the meet and</p>

<p>
<md>U+W</md>
</p>

<p>is the join.</p>
